<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Montoire-sur-le-Loir</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Montoire-sur-le-Loir is a small town in the Loir-et-Cher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. On 24 October 1940 Marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippe-petain">Philippe Pétain</a> met <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> at its railway station, and the handshake between them became the symbol of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> regime's policy of collaboration with Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, which Pétain announced in a radio broadcast a few days later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/montoire-sur-le-loir.jpg" alt="Montoire-sur-le-Loir" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Calips assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:France_Loir-et-Cher_Montoire-sur-le-Loir_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
